@tradition saturday-run
// Saturday run (FX14, 0.92.5 item 16; SW1's weekend pitch, the user's yes 2026-10-24): every other Saturday before the
// long breakfast, Dr. Nandakumar leads three easy laps of the promenade, the Lap of the Wren's loop. Behind WEEKEND_ON.
k: 458
title: Saturday run
// (the user, 2026-10-25: spread across weeks, two new a weekend; was: every 2 weeks saturday week 1)
when: every 4 weeks saturday week 1 from day 1
at: 07:00-07:40
min: 20
wake: 15
where: 3 pool @lap-of-the-wren
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
hold: none
who: nandakumar always, vance 70%, runner 50%, gym-regular 50%, early-riser 20%, everyone 5%
anim: talk
host: nandakumar
from: nandakumar

== mail
- Saturday run tomorrow at {time}. Three laps of the promenade, any speed. Then breakfast. Then water.

== ask
- Saturday run in the morning. Three laps. I'm aiming for two and a half.   #funny
- Running before breakfast with the doctor? She says it's good for us. She's usually right.
- Three slow laps, then pancakes. That's the deal I've made with myself.   #funny

== here
- Keep breathing. In, out. Any order you like.   #funny
- Lap two. Nearly there. Well. Nearly at lap three.   #funny
- Can you still talk? Then it's the right pace.
- Wave at the windows. Everyone else is still asleep.   #funny

== thanks
- You fall in with the Saturday runners: three easy laps of the promenade, the big windows going by, and the long breakfast waiting at the end.

== chatter
- Ran three laps before breakfast. Ate four pancakes after. That's balance.   #funny
- Vance turned up to the Saturday run with a stopwatch. Of course he did.   #funny
- The doctor runs the way she does everything. Calmly, and faster than you.   #warm
